{
 "version": 1,
 "contract": "AC-2a revision 3.2",
 "encoding": "lp(...) writes each part as its byte length (4 bytes, big-endian) then its bytes. Inside lp: text (labels, ids such as c_, r_, en_, ap_ and sr_ ids, actions, targets, emails, roles) as UTF-8; integers (seq, generation, requestedAt) as decimal ASCII; hashes (previewHash, a previous rosterHash or policyHash, the first being 32 zero bytes) as their raw 32 bytes; credentialId, cose, attestationObject, clientDataJSON, spki and serials as raw bytes. canonical_json is AC-1 3.6's (CE-1 with null). In JSON: hashes and fingerprints are lowercase hex; keys, certificates, MACs, nonces and signatures are base64url without padding; serials are lowercase hex; times are milliseconds. Every ECDSA signature is the ASN.1 DER ECDSA-Sig-Value.",
 "about": "4.6: challenge = SHA-256(lp(label, consoleId, action, target, canonical_json(params), canonical_json(targets))), targets [{relay, nonce}] sorted by relay id, nonce base64url of the relay's 32 random bytes; params the body without stepup. 4.7: request challenge = SHA-256(lp(label, consoleId, approvalId, action, target, canonical_json(params), canonical_json(relayIds sorted), requestedAt)); the approver's challenge is a 4.6 challenge with action approvals.approve and target the approval id. 4.4 and 4.5: hash(seq) = SHA-256(lp(label, consoleId, seq, hash(seq - 1), canonical_json(change or policy))), hash(0) 32 zero bytes; endorsement challenge SHA-256(lp(endorse label, consoleId, seq, hash(seq))). 4.1: scope request hash.",
